# Infinite scroll

Loads a page of todos, then loads the next page automatically whenever the
visitor scrolls to the bottom, until the server says there is nothing more.

## Note

`docs/frontend.md`'s Testing reference documents no drive verb for `When
the user scrolls to the bottom:` at all. The only way this lane found to
drive it is the UNDOCUMENTED `Raise "scrolledtobottom".` — found only by
reading `crates/logicaffeine_tests/tests/lgx_vm_parity_lock.rs`'s own
`scrolling_to_the_bottom_reaches_its_handler_on_both_tiers` — the same class
of gap as `examples/file_drop_upload`'s G25 for a file drop's own
undocumented drive verb. Recorded as finding G26,
`work/lgx-ease/gauntlet2.md` (a documentation gap, no RED test needed: the
mechanism works once found, unlike G25's `(file: File)`).

## A Todo has:
    an id, which is Int.
    a text, which is Text.
    a done, which is Bool.

## To countLoaded (todos: Seq of Todo) -> Int:
    Return length of todos.

## Page /

State:
    Let todos be a new Seq of Todo.
    Let error be "".
    Let pageNum be 1.
    Let exhausted be false.
    Let loadedCount always be countLoaded(todos).

Actions:
    When the page loads:
        Get "/api/todos" as Seq of Todo, then loaded.

    To loaded (answer: Result of Seq of Todo and HttpError):
        Inspect answer:
            When Ok (list):
                Let mutable merged be todos.
                Repeat for t in list:
                    Push t to merged.
                Set todos to merged.
                Set error to "".
                If length of list is equal to 0:
                    Set exhausted to true.
            When Err (e):
                Set error to e's message.
                Set exhausted to true.

    When the user scrolls to the bottom:
        If exhausted is equal to false:
            Set pageNum to pageNum + 1.
            Get "/api/todos2" as Seq of Todo, then loaded.

View:
    <main>
      <h1>Todos <small id="count">({loadedCount})</small></h1>
      {if error is not "":}<p class="error" role="alert">{error}</p>{end}
      <ul class="todos">
        {for each t in todos:}
          <li>{t's text}</li>
        {else:}
          <li class="empty">Nothing to do.</li>
        {end}
      </ul>
      <p id="status">{if exhausted:}no more todos{end}</p>
    </main>

Style:
    main { max-width: 34rem; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
    h1 { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: .6rem; }
    h1 small { font-size: .85rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); }
    .error { color: var(--danger); font-weight: 600; }
    .todos { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    .empty { color: var(--muted); padding: .45rem 0; }

## Test: the first page loads on mount

Given that GET "/api/todos" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 1, \"text\": \"milk\", \"done\": false}}]".
Expect that the count of ".todos li" is equal to 1.
Expect that the text of "#count" is equal to "(1)".

## Test: scrolling to the bottom loads the next page and appends it

Given that GET "/api/todos" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 1, \"text\": \"milk\", \"done\": false}}]".
Given that GET "/api/todos2" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 2, \"text\": \"bread\", \"done\": false}}]".
Raise "scrolledtobottom".
Expect that the count of ".todos li" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#count" is equal to "(2)".

## Test: an empty page marks the feed exhausted and stops further loads

Given that GET "/api/todos" answers 200 with "[{{\"id\": 1, \"text\": \"milk\", \"done\": false}}]".
Given that GET "/api/todos2" answers 200 with "[]".
Raise "scrolledtobottom".
Expect that the text of "#status" is equal to "no more todos".
Expect that the count of ".todos li" is equal to 1.

